`x <= 0 && floor(x) == x`.  Non-integer arguments are untouched: the
existing vectors at -1.5, -10.5, -100.5 and -262144.5, and the complex
points at (-1.5, 5.0) and (-20.5, -20.5), all return the same values as
before.  With the change reverted `specfunc_test` reports 11 failures, all
of them the new vectors.

**This corrects a mistake of mine.**  The patch in Savannah bug #58066
widened the digamma check to exactly this predicate, and I recorded it in
the review notes as a regression, reasoning that the three named values
were the intended set.  They are not: the set of poles is the set of
non-positive integers, and the reporter was right.  The finding came out of
